-- Coherence accept (FQN dispatch Stage 1): two DISTINCT types that share the
-- short name `Thing`, declared in different (nested) modules, may each implement
-- a TYPE-DISPATCHED BUILTIN interface (Eq) — coherence keys on the DECLARING
-- MODULE, so the distinct types do NOT overlap. This is sound compiled because
-- Eq/Ord/Show/Hash dispatch natively through generated ctor-qualified structural
-- functions (ensure_adt_eq_fn), not the bare-type-name mangling that a general
-- user interface uses. Regression for the bare-name coherence key
-- (AeLib.AeDir vs AeLib2.AeDir). Reject twin for a GENERAL interface: reject/t82.
mod Top do
  mod NA do
    type Thing = TA
    impl Eq(Thing) do
      fn eq(x, y) do eq(x, y) end
    end
  end
  mod NB do
    type Thing = TB
    impl Eq(Thing) do
      fn eq(x, y) do eq(x, y) end
    end
  end
  fn main() do 0 end
end
